  "details": "Ever since the new menu & params editors were pushed to mainline this oversight keeps popping up and requiring one to clear fields via debug view. It's annoying. Clear it either on SDK control panel repaint or on UI repaint.\n\nFiling under bug report because hunting down invisible params is not the top notch UX.\n\nReplication:\n\n1. Make a menu, create an item in it\n\n2. Switch that item to something that has any conditional fields rendering, such as menu asset reference field, sub parameters, or labels\n\n3. Fill those in\n\n4. Switch back to something that doesn't render conditional fields, such as Toggle type\n\nThis preserves set values or references. Typically not an issue, except changed parameters will remain unlisted, and will validation errors, preventing one from building the avatar. You also do not need to reference an asset that is not used.\n\nPossible fixes:\n\n1. Clear hidden fields when the type changes, introduce the undo history support\n\n2. Clear hidden fields when the validator runs\n\n3. Clear hidden fields on build, add validator checks to avoid confusing errors",
